# Step 1 — OSS Assessment

Use APP_NAME, HIGHLIGHT_NAME, and HIGHLIGHT_APP_ID already resolved
in this conversation. Do not ask the user to re-enter them.
If any are missing from context, say so and stop — do not guess.

Follow #file:.github/skills/highlight-data-fetch.md exactly for Steps 0 and 1.

Key notes:
- Step 0 of the skill uses HIGHLIGHT_APP_ID (integer) for cache refresh.
- nature=third_parties returns safe upgrade versions directly — use them.
- nature=licenses returns license risk — fetch this too.

## Flag each component
- 🔴 CRITICAL — CVSS ≥ 9 or KEV
- 🟠 HIGH — CVSS 7–8.9
- 🟡 MEDIUM — CVSS 4–6.9
- ⚠️ LICENSE — GPL, AGPL, LGPL, unknown
- 📅 OUTDATED — newer stable version exists, no CVE

A component can carry multiple flags.

## Prioritise
- P1 = any 🔴 CRITICAL
- P2 = any 🟠 HIGH, no CRITICAL
- P3 = 🟡 MEDIUM, ⚠️ LICENSE, or 📅 OUTDATED only

## Write oss_remediation_plan.md

```md
# OSS Remediation Plan — <HIGHLIGHT_NAME>

| | |
|---|---|
| Highlight snapshot date | <lastAnalysisDate> |
| Snapshot label          | <snapshotLabel> |
| Report generated        | <now> |
| Source                  | CAST Highlight MCP — live scan, no cache |

